1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:05,839
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

2
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:11,052
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:16,641
- ♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

4
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:20,645
[Tikboy] Only a few people were going
in and out of that shop.

5
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:22,772
Maybe more than twenty.

6
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,899
Someone arrived. Handsome!

7
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:26,943
- But he was locked out.
- [metal clangs]

8
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:30,947
- [gunshot]
- [Tikboy] Then I heard… like gunfire.

9
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,366
We brought out two wounded people.

10
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,285
Then suddenly, boom!

11
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:37,162
[Atoy] Do you know why this happened?

12
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:38,997
Did Samir take them all?

13
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,875
The last thing Sir Mercado told me,

14
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:48,089
he had a big mission to announce
about Belladonna and Obsidian.

15
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:51,259
Come with me to the precinct,
I'll question you there.

16
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:53,720
Ah, sorry. I won't go with you.

17
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,181
I have a balloon

18
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:58,600
All right. Ah, I'll come back later.

19
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,269
Sir Atoy, I'm really worried
about Sir Mercado,

20
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:03,354
because he's like a father to me.

21
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:05,690
If you had arrived at the
party on time, maybe--

22
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,984
Maybe I wouldn't be here now.

23
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,736
[Atoy] You can rest here for now.

24
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,529
I have to hide you here for now.

25
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,907
I told my family I'm retired.

26
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,326
[Samir, in English]
30 trackers on manifest.

27
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,995
One in the hospital, Uno Alcaraz.

28
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:22,207
It's 29. That means we're
missing somebody.

29
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:27,295
I have a bad feeling, Anthony Padua
is still out there.

30
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:29,964
[Atoy] Mercado left me a note, he said…

31
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,550
[Atoy, in English] "Protect the Belladonna
at all costs."

32
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:34,928
Maybe it's a code name?

33
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:38,765
That's exactly what I'll find out
from Samir, before I kill him.

34
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:40,391
["Fix this"] ♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

35
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:46,523
[pan sizzling]

36
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,819
- [in English] Good morning, Gavin!
- [in English] Good morning!

37
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:53,655
Best morning ever,

38
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:56,324
waking up and you're
the first person I see.

39
00:01:57,158 --> 00:02:02,038
[light music playing]

40
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,881
[Cita] Poor guy, huh?

41
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:14,801
[Atoy] Yes, Godmother. Geez.

42
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,097
Gavin, what are you doing?

43
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,517
Ah, I'm just looking for something to eat.

44
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,311
Something to eat?

45
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,568
You're going to eat raw squash?

46
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:34,320
There's bread.

47
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:36,239
Ah, that's better.

48
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:41,035
We already talked about the rules.

49
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:42,954
You're finding ways around them.

50
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:45,540
No, Miss Cita. No.

51
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:49,502
'Mom, your rules are so over the top that
we can't even be near each other.

52
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:53,798
What if I'm drowning, and Gavin
is the closest to me.

53
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:56,593
What? He can't come near me?

54
00:02:56,676 --> 00:03:00,221
Drowning? Where would you drown,
in a bucket?

55
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,890
Here in the sink? In the toilet?

56
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:04,058
Hey, we don't have a swimming pool here.

57
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:06,603
Karla, Gavin…

58
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:11,065
we can't always watch you
inside the house.

59
00:03:12,483 --> 00:03:17,614
So, you should always do what's right
even when no one's looking.

60
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,365
Okay?

61
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:21,534
Yes, Big Brother Atoy.

62
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:27,206
Ah, Brother, can you call Uno?

63
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,251
T-Bak invited him to play basketball,

64
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:32,795
but since last night he hasn't
texted, hasn't replied.

65
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:35,882
Karla, didn't you hear?

66
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:39,594
Uno was shot last night at the event
he attended with Atoy.

67
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:41,346
What?!

68
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:43,806
[pensive music playing]

69
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:47,435
OMG, Brother! There was an explosion?

70
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:48,770
Your boss died?

71
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:52,440
Brother, it says here, gas leak was the
reason for the explosion.

72
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,441
Is that true?

73
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:58,196
Wait. It says here,
it was a terrorist attack.

74
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:02,075
Samir's group attacked
the event last night.

75
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:04,244
[music continues]

76
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:07,288
Whatever you see there, that's
not what really happened.

77
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:10,792
Maybe the media is just covering up,
so people won't panic.

78
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:14,879
But the police are already investigating.

79
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,882
Brother, what's your plan now?

80
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:20,134
Your mortal enemy is back!

81
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:23,346
Nothing. I'm retired, remember?

82
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:26,516
[human sound]
And Samir has another target anyway.

83
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:28,851
Let the police handle it.

84
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:33,022
[Cita] It's better you don't get involved.

85
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:36,192
Let's just pray Uno recovers.

86
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:45,034
[music swells]

87
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:47,078
[theme music playing]

88
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:49,497
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor…</i> ♪

89
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:52,166
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

90
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:57,714
♪ <i>Wait a moment, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

91
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,882
♪ <i>Can you be the one to sew</i> ♪

92
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,259
["My polo's hole"] ♪ <i>My polo's hole</i> ♪

93
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,261
♪ <i>that fits just under the armpit</i> ♪

94
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:05,263
♪ <i>In every cut of cloth</i> ♪

95
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,015
♪ <i>There's a secret behind it</i> ♪

96
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:08,933
♪ <i>If your measurement is wrong,</i> ♪

97
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:13,479
♪ <i>the whole fit turns crooked…</i> ♪

98
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,940
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

99
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,192
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

100
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,779
["Fix this"] ♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

101
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,284
You were right…

102
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:30,079
more than twenty bodies are missing?

103
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:31,414
Wait a minute.

104
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:33,333
Are they all relatives…

105
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,959
of Mr. Mercado?

106
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,085
No, Sir.

107
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,504
They have different jobs and backgrounds.

108
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:41,049
Remi De Dios, a baker in Bulacan.

109
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,177
Lobert Villa, a barber in Laguna.

110
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:47,346
Ronalyn Tapales, a saleslady in Cebu.

111
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,973
The common denominator:

112
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:52,643
all of them had military
backgrounds from different years.

113
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:57,565
But some of them were professionally
trained in combat.

114
00:05:57,648 --> 00:06:01,819
Like Uno Alcaraz, who until now…
is still unconscious in the ICU.

115
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:05,239
[in English] But wait, there's more.

116
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,408
Oh?

117
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:10,203
Some victims were illegal aliens.

118
00:06:10,286 --> 00:06:11,913
Foreigners without papers.

119
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:17,043
Hmm. Interesting.

120
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:19,420
And also, Sir,

121
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:23,633
there is a medico-legal report on
a body found outside the venue;

122
00:06:23,716 --> 00:06:25,968
cyanide poisoning is the cause
of death, Sir.

123
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:31,516
Hmm. It's giving me spy vibes.

124
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:33,601
Or a terrorist who was cornered,

125
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:35,895
refused to give information,

126
00:06:35,978 --> 00:06:38,940
and chose to die with the secrets
he carried.

127
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:45,279
[sneaky music playing]

128
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:47,490
- [in English] Oh, excuse me.
- Yes?

129
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:50,368
Where is the female patient admitted
here yesterday?

130
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:55,039
The survivor from the Gregorio explosion,
because I need to investigate her.

131
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,707
- Who?
- The woman…

132
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:59,085
beautiful, slim.

133
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:01,712
Her lips are as big as her chest.

134
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,549
Jane Doe?

135
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:05,967
[suspicious music playing]

136
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:10,388
She was taken home by the man who
brought her here last night.

137
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:13,057
The one who looks like Marimar's husband?

138
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:16,561
- Yes, that guy.
- Yes. Yes, Sir. That's him.

139
00:07:17,854 --> 00:07:19,605
Why did you allow it?

140
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,566
I said don't let her leave,

141
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:24,277
because I need to question her
about what happened.

142
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,864
You know, I have doubts about that man.

143
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:30,783
Hmm.

144
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:33,744
Shugo, I have something for you to do.

145
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:36,956
[music fades]

146
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,833
Ah, are you listening?

147
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:40,793
Uhm, I need to pass through.

148
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:41,919
You're blocking the way.

149
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,546
[in English] Ah, sorry.

150
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:52,180
Son.

151
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:53,931
- Oh?
- [Atoy] Oh, bro?

152
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:55,725
What are you doing here?

153
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,977
Don't you have work?

154
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,145
No, there are plenty of them there anyway.

155
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:00,313
Let them handle that.

156
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:03,524
I came to see you because…

157
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:07,528
I want to help you with
your secret mission.

158
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,571
What?

159
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:11,282
Do you have any idea how
you'll find Samir?

160
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:15,995
[pensive music playing]

161
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:17,705
I went to Lily,

162
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:20,458
had her unlock the passcode on this phone.

163
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:21,834
[music swells]

164
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,586
Whose phone is that?

165
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:26,506
Samir's man.

166
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:29,634
[suspicious music playing]

167
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:32,887
[Foreign man on the phone, in English]
<i>Evacuate your positions.</i>

168
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:37,183
<i>The bombs are in place.</i>
<i>Samir and Artem are already secured.</i>

169
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:40,102
[music fades]

170
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:45,358
What will you do?

171
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:46,442
[speaker id] You'll call Samir?

172
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:52,823
Wait.

173
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:56,744
Here.

174
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:59,205
[music continues]

175
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:00,540
[in English] Red…

176
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:05,753
- [in English] Blossom.
- Blossom, 7 PM.

177
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:07,463
That's in one day.

178
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,257
[in English] Red Blossom.

179
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,968
[in English] Blossom, Red Blossom.

180
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:13,886
[clicks tongue] That place…

181
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,680
I've been there.

182
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,391
[Emerson] Ah, it's like--

183
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:21,102
a high-end, for the wealthy,
Japanese restaurant.

184
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:23,229
One of the owners was my client.

185
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,565
[music continues]

186
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,775
The staff there,

187
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:30,194
the servers, they wear…

188
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:32,655
Japanese-style clothing for…

189
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:34,031
- Geisha?
- Geisha, geisha!

190
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,992
They're dressed like that.

191
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:38,911
Emerson, help me.

192
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,496
[tense music playing]

193
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,290
I'll take care of you.

194
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:48,254
[music continues]

195
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:50,631
[lively chatter]

196
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:51,841
[in English] Sorry.

197
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:55,970
I[byang] I feel awkward around
our classmates.

198
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:58,556
They all speak English,

199
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:00,516
like they're cartoons.

200
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,602
No one speaks Tagalog!

201
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,188
They're rich, that's why.

202
00:10:06,272 --> 00:10:08,065
And excuse me,

203
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,358
we know how to speak English too.

204
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:10,610
Don't let them beat you at it.

205
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:13,279
[sneaky music playing]

206
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:19,076
Anyway, if you don't understand
what they're saying,

207
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:21,078
because they speak too fast,

208
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,455
this is what you'll say, okay?

209
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,372
Watch me.

210
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:26,584
Pretend I'm the English-speaking person
you're talking to.

211
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,377
[human sound]

212
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:29,545
[in English] Excuse me.

213
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,464
I beg your pardon.

214
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:34,550
In slow motion, please.

215
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:36,177
Like that! Like that.

216
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,095
[Janine] Like that. [chuckles]

217
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,847
That's how you say it?

218
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,474
Why does it sound straight?

219
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:43,184
Like it's just one word.

220
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:45,061
Yes, that's how it is.

221
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:46,812
They say it's more boujie

222
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:50,066
when it lacks vowels and is straight.

223
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,984
[Janine] I'll just buy drinks. You?

224
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,404
Buy me sticky balls in coconut milk.

225
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:56,614
It's so good.

226
00:10:57,239 --> 00:10:59,075
I gotchu, Ibyang Sinulid.

227
00:10:59,158 --> 00:10:59,992
I'll be back.

228
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:03,037
[music continues]

229
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:09,126
[music fades]

230
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:15,299
Hmm.

231
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,637
[human sound]

232
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:25,226
[music]

233
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:29,021
[in English] Hi! I'm Hailey!

234
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:33,484
You and your sister are transferees
from a public school, right?

235
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:35,736
Are you guys poor or something?

236
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:39,073
Like you eat dove or pigeons
for breakfast?

237
00:11:39,156 --> 00:11:40,408
Uhm…

238
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,577
[in English] Excuse me.

239
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:47,123
I beg your pardon.

240
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:50,876
In slow motion.

241
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:54,463
[in English] What? You are so weird.

242
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:55,548
[music continues]

243
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:56,632
And eww!

244
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:58,926
What's that?

245
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:00,553
Is that rotten food?

246
00:12:00,636 --> 00:12:01,595
You eat garbage?

247
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:03,347
[music fades]

248
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:06,559
[in English] No! It's mung beans!

249
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:09,395
It's very nutritious and super yummy!

250
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:14,442
And-- and we don't
eat pigeons for breakfast!

251
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,903
[in English] Now, have you seen it?

252
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:18,988
[in English] Seen what?

253
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:21,615
[in English] My appetite!

254
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:24,452
I lost it because of your rotten mouth!

255
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:26,745
[music continues]

256
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:27,788
[human sound]

257
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:39,383
- Ouch.
- Deserve!

258
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,593
That hurts.

259
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:42,428
[sneaky music playing]

260
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:43,679
Mmm-hmm.

261
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,184
[sewing machine whirring]

262
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,105
Ah…

263
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,982
- Sir Atoy.
- Hmm?

264
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:57,193
- Oh, thanks.
- Coffee.

265
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:58,611
- Thanks.
- Oh.

266
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:01,280
[sneaky music playing]

267
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:02,573
Sir Atoy, is this for me?

268
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:05,284
- [Atoy] Hmm?
- Perfect, I don't have clothes anymore.

269
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:07,369
- This is for you, yeah.
- [sound]

270
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:09,371
No, I'll use this for…

271
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,664
a job.

272
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:13,250
Anyway, I'll just give you money.

273
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:15,377
Go to the thrift store, buy clothes.

274
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:17,630
- [Jesabel] Ahh.
- There's one on the corner.

275
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:19,715
- I'll take care of you.
- Too bad, it's nice.

276
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:21,467
- I want that too.
- 'Toy?

277
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:23,844
- Get the fabric-- Oh, 'Son?
- [Emerson] Ah…

278
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:26,347
I already talked to Red Blossom.

279
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:28,307
They said they have a foreign guest

280
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,391
at seven o'clock.

281
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:30,768
So, I think it's…

282
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:33,020
Samir--

283
00:13:33,103 --> 00:13:34,396
[sneaky music playing]

284
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,649
- [Atoy] Ah. Ah…
- Ah, who-- who is she?

285
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:37,566
[speaker id]

286
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:41,362
Emerson, Jesabel. Jesabel, ah…

287
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,822
- My best friend, Emerson.
- Ah, friend, friend.

288
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,575
Yes. She's Colonel Mercado's secretary.

289
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:48,202
Uncle Emerson!

290
00:13:48,285 --> 00:13:49,578
I'm a tracker in training.

291
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,413
You're a tracker too?

292
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:52,665
[music continues]

293
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:56,293
- [Atoy] Ah…
- [titters] "Uncle"? "Uncle," really?

294
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,170
Uncle.

295
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,130
Well, not exactly. She's good too.

296
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:01,632
She's also very capable.

297
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:03,133
She was one of those injured at the party.

298
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:04,969
[Atoy] I'm letting her stay here for now.

299
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,596
Oh, by the way.

300
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,849
We'll talk about your training later.

301
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:13,394
If you see Godmother Cita

302
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:14,770
and Ame,

303
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,021
tell them you're…

304
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,400
a bedspacer here.

305
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:22,820
That you're renting the room.

306
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:28,617
Uhm, also say you'll help with chores,
that you agreed to do that.

307
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,494
- Ah, I'll be a helper first?
- Yes, something like that.

308
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,204
- Okay.
- I'll talk to them too.

309
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,581
All right, all right.

310
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:35,040
[music fades]

311
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,710
So… So-- [clears throat] So…

312
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:40,504
No one should know who she really is?

313
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,047
Uh-huh.

314
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,632
[in English] Secret tracker.

315
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:44,592
[Emerson] Uh-huh.

316
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:47,511
- Okay. Noted.
- Okay?

317
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:50,347
- [Emerson] Okay.
- [sneaky music playing]

318
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,683
- [Atoy] Is she brave?
- Yeah.

319
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:55,019
[chuckles] Oh, that's not yours--

320
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:57,062
That's his! I made that.

321
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,815
[music continues]

322
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,442
[Janine] Ibyang!

323
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:02,693
Ibyang!

324
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:06,071
Ibyang.

325
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,323
Are you okay?

326
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:09,325
[human sound] I'm fine.

327
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,993
- Are you sure?
- I'm fine, I'm fine.

328
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:13,412
I saw it. Our classmate tripped you.

329
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:16,165
I'll really confront that one.

330
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:17,541
- Where is that person?
- Hey, hey, hey.

331
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:19,335
Don't, don't, don't, don't, don't.

332
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:25,132
Janine, Mama once said,

333
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:27,927
bullies usually have problems at home.

334
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,971
That's why they take it out at school.

335
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:33,432
So what?

336
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:35,059
And besides, I'm the only one

337
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,936
allowed to bully you, okay? Hello?

338
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,103
I don't care.

339
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:39,939
I'll confront that one.

340
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:43,317
Don't, Janine!

341
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:46,153
Ibyang, why are we even

342
00:15:46,236 --> 00:15:49,823
thread and needle for life,
if the needle won't act

343
00:15:49,907 --> 00:15:51,450
when its thread is hurt?

344
00:15:53,369 --> 00:16:00,334
Janine, because the thread
wants its needle to be good.

345
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,337
So, promise me

346
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,839
you won't retaliate, okay?

347
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,925
Don't do it!

348
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:09,468
Okay, fine.

349
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:10,928
But if it happens again,

350
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:12,596
I'll really make them pay.

351
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,641
All right, let's go back to class.

352
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,851
Wait. You go ahead.

353
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:19,520
I'll look for the restroom.

354
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,188
Okay. The restroom's over there.

355
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:22,398
Okay.

356
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:25,234
[mellow music playing]

357
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:27,152
[muffled chattering]

358
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:34,410
[mysterious music playing]

359
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:46,046
[music fades]

360
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:51,510
[door hinge squeaking]

361
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:55,514
[sneaky music playing]

362
00:16:55,597 --> 00:16:56,765
[door closes]

363
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:01,395
[music continues]

364
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:28,255
[music fades]

365
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:37,056
[sneaky music playing]

366
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:50,152
[music continues]

367
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:58,952
[car engine revving] [horn honks]

368
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:15,302
Oh? Shall we go?

369
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,263
[in English] Ready?

370
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:20,432
Ah, what about…

371
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:22,309
Jesabel, isn't she coming?

372
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:24,394
Jesabel?

373
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,188
Why?

374
00:18:27,272 --> 00:18:28,482
What, do you like Jesabel?

375
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:29,775
What--

376
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:31,443
- what do you mean I like her?
- Yes, of course.

377
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:34,071
No-- no! It's just--

378
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:36,532
No, no way. I was just asking.

379
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,658
Oh?

380
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:39,409
And besides, I already have

381
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,161
Denden, My Loves.

382
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,538
Maybe she likes me.

383
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:44,248
Whoa.

384
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:45,290
[chuckles]

385
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:47,417
I won't bring her along, it's risky.

386
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,295
The police seem to be watching us.

387
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,588
They got eyes on her.

388
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:53,757
So, she has to lay low.

389
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,759
[sneaky music playing]

390
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:56,718
He likes you, huh.

391
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,011
Maybe she does!

392
00:18:58,095 --> 00:18:59,304
Don't accuse me, 'Toy, okay.

393
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:00,597
- [Emerson] Let's go.
- [chuckles]

394
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:07,062
- [chuckles]
- [car doors closing]

395
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:13,402
[suspicious music playing]

396
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:19,491
[car engine revving]

397
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:23,745
[music continues]

398
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:28,125
[lively chatter]

399
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:33,380
- Hi!
- [muffled chattering]

400
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:37,843
Where did you come from?

401
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:41,597
Why are you smiling like that?

402
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,892
Me? Nothing, just happy.

403
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,102
Oh, by the way,

404
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,479
the sticky rice balls in coconut milk
I asked you to buy.

405
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:50,981
Did you keep it?

406
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,900
I'll eat it later.

407
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,194
I left it outside.

408
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:57,321
I'll get it back when it's there, okay.

409
00:19:58,322 --> 00:20:01,408
[sneaky music playing]

410
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:10,751
[in English] Everyone, please have a seat!

411
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:14,504
[chairs scraping]

412
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:16,006
[in English] Good morning, everyone!

413
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:19,927
[Students, in English]
Good morning, Ms. Magno!

414
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,637
[in English] All right. Have a seat,

415
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,388
and please get your notebook number 5.

416
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:30,020
[music continues]

417
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,189
[in English] Where's my cat keychain?

418
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:40,614
[music swells]

419
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,532
[in English] Teacher!

420
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:45,494
My things! My books!
They're all soiled and wet!

421
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:49,206
[Students] Eww!

422
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,833
Eww! Is that vomit?!

423
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:53,335
[Student 2] It's so gross!

424
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,128
[indistinct chattering]

425
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,713
Eww!

426
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:59,007
[in English] Everyone,
please take your seats!

427
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,510
[lively chatter]

428
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:03,762
[Teacher, in English] It's okay.
Let me get your bag outside. Okay?

429
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:07,140
[lively chatter]

430
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:11,603
[pensive music playing]

431
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:31,248
Janine?

432
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,794
- Janine.
- Ibyang.

433
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:39,423
Janine, I have to ask you something.

434
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:42,217
[human sound] Are you sure…

435
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:44,469
you left the sticky rice balls
in coconut milk outside,

436
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:48,390
and didn't throw it inside Hailey's bag?

437
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:51,310
Psst! Don't say anything.

438
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:55,188
- [human sound]
- Hmm. I knew it!

439
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:57,899
Why did you do that? That's wrong.

440
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:01,153
Why? She deserved it.

441
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,821
And I won't allow

442
00:22:02,904 --> 00:22:05,240
anyone to bully you just like that!

443
00:22:05,824 --> 00:22:06,867
[in English] Okay.

444
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:11,747
Thank you for thinking of me.

445
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:16,293
But it's still wrong.

446
00:22:16,376 --> 00:22:18,462
Didn't you promise me?

447
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:21,214
Apologize to her.

448
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,925
You want me to admit I did that?

449
00:22:24,676 --> 00:22:25,886
[Janine] No way!

450
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,804
If I admit it,

451
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:29,848
she'll tell the teacher!

452
00:22:30,557 --> 00:22:33,310
If you won't admit it…

453
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:37,022
then don't do it again, okay.

454
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:39,316
[human sound]

455
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:42,402
And let's just be her friend.

456
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:44,863
Because earlier I saw that…

457
00:22:44,946 --> 00:22:47,240
it seems she has no friends.

458
00:22:47,324 --> 00:22:48,909
[scoffs]

459
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:50,035
Ibyang…

460
00:22:50,911 --> 00:22:53,205
Friend? No.

461
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:55,165
Just you.

462
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:57,501
Don't include me in that.

463
00:22:58,251 --> 00:23:01,129
And don't order me around.

464
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:04,508
Just because you're the real
child, I have to obey?

465
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:07,135
Oh, really?

466
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:10,347
Do you want me to tell Tatoy?

467
00:23:10,430 --> 00:23:14,810
[human sound]
Don't. Don't tell on me, please.

468
00:23:16,686 --> 00:23:18,063
Okay, fine!

469
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:19,689
Tomorrow, for you,

470
00:23:19,773 --> 00:23:23,360
I'll return the cat keychain I took.

471
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:24,736
What?

472
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,571
Cat keychain?

473
00:23:27,614 --> 00:23:29,699
Why did you take it? That's bad!

474
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:31,201
She's bad too!

475
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,410
So we're even.

476
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,204
[Janine] Okay, fine.

477
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:36,748
Tomorrow, I'll make it up to her.

478
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:38,625
[in English] Promise.

479
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:40,127
[in English] Promise?

480
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:41,461
[in English] Promise.

481
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:42,629
All right.

482
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:44,005
- [light music playing]
- Let's go.

483
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,257
Come on.

484
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:49,302
[music fades]

485
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:57,435
Sir, ah, I'm Emerson Mendoza.

486
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:59,855
I'm Mr. Komatsu's tailor.

487
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:02,983
Ah, is my friend done?

488
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:05,152
Yes, I already interviewed her,

489
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:06,820
and I also processed her bio data.

490
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:07,988
Where is she?

491
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:10,073
Has she been dressed in kimono?

492
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,283
Made up already?

493
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:12,909
Yes, earlier.

494
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,035
Here she is.

495
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,036
Antonia! Come here.

496
00:24:16,663 --> 00:24:17,873
[light music playing]

497
00:24:17,956 --> 00:24:20,041
This is Antonia.

498
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:22,586
Sir…

499
00:24:22,669 --> 00:24:24,838
[giggles] That's Antonia.

500
00:24:24,921 --> 00:24:26,673
[chuckles]

501
00:24:26,756 --> 00:24:27,924
- Good evening!
- Good evening.

502
00:24:29,259 --> 00:24:31,011
You won't use your real name.

503
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:34,472
Your name will be Atsuyo.

504
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:38,393
Ohh. [giggles]

505
00:24:38,476 --> 00:24:40,228
Atsuyo. [chuckles]

506
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,438
Atsuyo!

507
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:45,734
[in English] Anyway, your assigned guests
will arrive in 15 minutes.

508
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:50,113
You and Deiko will be serving
in the Tatami Room C

509
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,948
under Mr. Danny Guo's group.

510
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:53,158
Hmm. Hai.

511
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:54,492
Okay?

512
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,661
[rock music playing]

513
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:58,997
[human sound]

514
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:04,794
[electronic blipping]

515
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:09,007
[intense music playing]

516
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:10,550
Does she really have to dress like that?

517
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:13,678
Her papaya is almost spilling out,

518
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:15,305
you could just pick it.

519
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:17,140
And her shorts, they're full of holes.

520
00:25:17,224 --> 00:25:18,808
What's that? Bitten by rats?

521
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,227
You're so cute when you're angry

522
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:22,229
and jealous at the same time.

523
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,563
Psst.

524
00:25:23,647 --> 00:25:24,814
- [chuckles, then gasps] Oh, child.
- Hey!

525
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,358
- Karla.
- [Karla] Gavin!

526
00:25:26,441 --> 00:25:28,235
We're not allowed in one room, remember?

527
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:30,028
And you're not allowed to come near me.

528
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:31,154
[thuds]

529
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:33,156
What are you doing?!

530
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,491
I'll come along,

531
00:25:34,574 --> 00:25:37,118
because I heard you and Emerson last night

532
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:39,704
saying you'll track Samir's lead.

533
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:41,623
- Oh?
- You need me.

534
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:43,833
[speaker id] Godmother, this is Oka.

535
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:45,043
Good evening, Ma'am.

536
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:46,169
Sir-- Sir Oscar?

537
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:47,337
Don't leave yet,

538
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,297
even if you've recovered
already because…

539
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:51,132
when Sir Atoy is busy,

540
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:53,093
I'll ask you to teach me

541
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:54,552
to be a good tracker.

542
00:25:55,178 --> 00:25:56,638
Tracker? What's that?

543
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:58,556
[music swells]

544
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,684
Fix this
